      "writtenOn": "2023-07-27T16:28:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the goal is to eventually make this actually return a const thing, probably shouldn\u0027t use `glyph.mask()` and instead...\n\n    SkMask mask;\n    mask.fImage \u003d imageBuffer;\n    mask.fBounds \u003d glyph.iRect();\n    mask.fRowBytes \u003d glyph.rowBytes();\n    mask.fFormat \u003d glyph.maskFormat();\n\nWhile at the moment this produces exactly the same as `glyph.mask()` it would be nice to do this so that we can clean up and not set the `glyph.fImage` until after the image is created in `imageBuffer` (in which case `glyph.mask().fImage` would be nullptr here).",
      "revId": "4b92f9ad18116f46fb930285b9e5327955c5861e",
